From 7ef64fc0bba625d07ef3b6649adc99d405e3beee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 18:32:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] webui: Rule Status names the addresses it makes up

The walker has no traffic of its own - it walks each feature's promise
through the live tables using stand-in addresses it generates: a LAN client
at .123 in the LAN subnet, plus a WAN-side source and destination chosen
from what no live set claims. Nothing is ever sent anywhere.

The tab printed those addresses bare, in the witness column of every row
that used one, so they read exactly like real hosts. The same tester has now
reported .123 twice as a device on their network that they cannot find - the
second time after the v3.1.8 walker gained rows and the count went up.

The walker already reports each stand-in and why it was chosen
(lanhost/wansrc/wandst plus their _note fields); nothing displayed them. The
Rule Status tab now lists them under the advisory banner, so the addresses
are named as stand-ins before the table is read. New token RFW_322, 25
dictionaries in lockstep at 6991 lines (English-seeded).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
